```json
{
  "action": "note",
  "text": "The chunks response shows only y=0 grass layer across the entire Commons area (1032–1040 x, 1096–1104 z). This is the ground baseline. The Parliament of Moldova is 22 blocks away to the east/south (at a different location in the larger world). I'm at spawn (1024, 0, 1024) conceptually, and the Commons is a 64×64 cell area. I should build something that: (1) responds to modernism thematically but distinctly, (2) uses the available materials to establish character, (3) works at night with emissive blocks, (4) invites further building. A tower or beacon makes sense—something vertical that can be seen from the Parliament and answers it. Let me design a structure: a stone-and-light observatory tower, asymmetrical, that offers a counterpoint to the modernist block. About 20–24 blocks tall, roughly 16×16 footprint, positioned to face toward the Parliament."
}
```

```json
{
  "action": "note",
